questions.questionText:
In a certain code language,

A + B means &lsquo;A is the sister of B&rsquo;

A - B means &lsquo;A is the husband of B&rsquo;

A × B means &lsquo;A is the son of B&rsquo;

A &divide; B means &lsquo;A is the daughter of B&rsquo;.

Based on the above, how is T related to S if &lsquo;T + P × M - V &divide; S&rsquo;?
